  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to COVID-19 effects in Guatemala: Strengthening the capacities of public institutions and increasing rural income</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to recover from the impact of COVID-19 the action seeks, on the one hand, to strengthen institutional capacities in the execution of public budgets related to FNS and social protection; and in the other to increase revenues among rural pop.Add. no. 1:Extension of the implementation or execution period: The operational implementation will be extended to 30 months; therefore, the execution period of the Action will be extended too. As defined in article 110 of the Financial Regulation (FR), the implementation period does not figure amongst the essential elements of a financing decision.Updates of the amounts/Reallocation of funds within the same action: Funds will be reallocated to be implemented through the indirect management modality. The total amount remains unchanged.Updates to the logical framework: The Action will be implemented as a whole Programme with two complementary sets of activities linked in a vertical logic. The provision of Technical Assistance will indeed be included in the secondary level commitment implemented in indirect management.Update of implementation modalities: Some activities will no longer be implemented through direct management but rather through the indirect management mode. The latter is already foreseen in the AD as an implementation mode.</narrative>
  </description>
